# Privacy of the site

Slates ships with **zero telemetry**. The public site must match.

- No Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, pixels, gtag, or “just a font counter”
- No third-party iframes; YouTube / tweets: link out, do not embed
- No cookie banners (there are no cookies we set)
- No Typekit / Google Fonts unless the face is **self-hosted**
- Do not add our own logs, measurement, or A/B tools

`/privacy` must say: local-first storage, **opt-in** iCloud, no app telemetry;
GitHub Pages may log request metadata at the infrastructure layer; we add
none. Support email (`mikedovale@pm.me`) is used only to reply.

Never claim “everything stays on your Mac” without the iCloud caveat:
**“Stored locally by default; optional iCloud sync.”**
